    {
      "id": "U-01",
      "question": "SUBMITTED is transient (\"caller never observes SUBMITTED at rest\", line 31) yet SUBMITTED→cancel is legal \"only reachable in the narrow window before gates resolve it\" (line 38). How can a test place a request in SUBMITTED to exercise the SUBMITTED row (including the legal cancel and the illegal submit/approve/reject/complete)? Is there a test hook, or should these cells be marked untestable?",
      "affects": [
        "ST-08",
        "ST-09",
        "ST-10",
        "ST-11",
        "ST-12",
        "ST-13",
        "ST-14"
